# ── Shared cPanel deploy (NO SSH) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Production is deployed by pulling this repo in cPanel with no terminal, so we
# CANNOT run `composer install` there. The framework itself must be committed:
#
#   /vendor  committed  — build locally with:
#                           composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader
#                         on the SAME PHP major.minor cPanel runs (8.3+),
#                         then commit it. The usual `/vendor` ignore is
#                         intentionally REMOVED. Do not re-add it unless the
#                         host gains a working Composer/terminal tool.
#
# Front-end note: this app renders server-side Blade with inline CSS and no
# @vite directive, so there are NO compiled assets and no `npm run build` step.
# /public/build stays ignored above (nothing is built into it).
#
# Still ignored:
#   .env             secrets — created by hand in cPanel File Manager, never committed
#   /public/storage  the storage symlink — recreated on the host (a committed
#                    symlink breaks across machines); see DEPLOYMENT.md
/public/storage
